there are two (2) wires. The specimen is received with a \u000amammogram. The specimen radiograph was examined. On the mammogram, multiple \u000afoci of calcifications are seen, as well as the clip. On sectioning, an area \u000aof biopsy cavity (2.2 x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm ) is identified. The clip is identified, and \u000atissue surrounding the clip is placed in microcassettes one and two. On \u000asectioning, no discrete masses are identified. Representative sections are \u000asubmitted for histologic analysis. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  tissue around clip, 1 frag/cass, ESS \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  representative sections of tissue around wire close to clip, \u000amulti frag, RSS \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  tissue around second wire, multi frag, RSS \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  additional breast tissue away from wires, multi frag, RSS \u000aafn \u000aReports to: OSTEEN, ROBERT, T. M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
