ich enters through \u000athe medial aspect of the specimen and exits through the lateral aspect of the \u000aspecimen. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol (superior red, inferior \u000agreen, medial orange, lateral yellow, anterior blue, posterior black), serially \u000asectioned from medial to lateral. The cut surface is tan/yellow and \u000ahomogeneous with focal areas of dense white fibrous tissue, which constitutes \u000aapproximately 70% of the breast parenchyma. No discrete lesions are grossly \u000aidentified. The specimen is submitted in its entirety. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial margin, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Sequential cross sections, medial to lateral, 2 frags each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral margin, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aBlocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  to include possible mass is noted per specimen radiograph. The \u000aspecimen radiograph is interpreted via Centricity and demonstrates the area of \u000ainterest marked by radiology. \u000aSEK/mmm \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000aFriday REMOVED_MONTH 27,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 09:21:12PM \u000aADDENDUM: \u000aDeeper histological levels on the intraductal papilloma present ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) show the \u000aatypical E-cadherin negative cells noted within the papilloma develop an \u000aapocrine appearance and have higher nuclear grade than typically seen in \u000aclassic ALH. These cells are  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID / REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  keratin positive and ER and PR negative \u000a(ER and PR negativity is commonly seen in apocrine lesions) and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID /neu \u000anegative 