aVAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aPathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D. \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D. \u000a#1. LEFT BREAST EXCISION, WIRE LOCALIZED FOR A CLIP: \u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia with pagetoid spread. \u000aCysts with apocrine metaplasia. \u000aEpithelial hyperplasia. \u000aFocal fat necrosis suggestive of the prior core needle track (see note \u000abelow). \u000a#2. LEFT BREAST EXCISION: \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU is present (e.g. blocks 19, 20, 21) (see note \u000abelow). \u000aColumnar alteration of lobules with prominent apocrine snouts with atypia \u000a(block 24). \u000aCysts with apocrine metaplasia. \u000aSclerosing adenosis. \u000a#3. BREAST, MEDIAL WALL, RE-EXCISION: \u000aApocrine cysts (see note below). \u000aSclerosing adenosis. \u000aEpithelial hyperplasia. \u000aNOTE: The previously placed clip was not identified in the specimen \u000aradiographs. The fat necrosis in specimen #1 may identify the needle track, \u000abut does not definitively identify the biopsy site. Clinical correlation is \u000anecessary to determine if the specimens include the prior biopsy site. All \u000athree specimens were completely examined histologically and margins were \u000aevaluated microscopically. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: None given. \u000aOperation: Left breast needle directed biopsy. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Atypical ductal hyperplasia left breast. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left breast, re-excision site. \u000a2. Left breast, re-excision. \u000a3. Medial wall left breast. \u000aSpecimen radiograph #1 - Clip is not in specimen. J. Leung, MD. \u000aSpecimen radiograph #2 - No clip in specimen. E.P. Frost. \u000aSpecimen radiograph #3 - No clip in specimen. E.P. Frost. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BENNETT,MICHAEL W.,M.B.,B.C.H \u000aThe specimen is received fresh in three parts, each  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient's \u000aname and unit number. \u000aPart one, labeled "#1, left breast, re-excision site", consists of a portion \u000aof fibrofatty tissue, which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.8cm  The specimen is inked \u000aper pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; \u000aanterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = \u000aorange. A localizing needle enters at the inferior border of the specimen. \u000aAt the posterior border of the specimen is a cyst, which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x \u000a0.5cm  Approximately 70% of the specimen consists of white fibrotic tissue, \u000awhich extends to all the margins of the specimen. The specimen is serially \u000asectioned from superior to inferior and entirely submitted for microscopic \u000aexamination. The area of needle tip localization is included in cassette 10. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  entire specimen, superior to inferior, 15 frags, ESS. \u000aPart two, labeled "#2, left breast, re-excision", consists of a portion of \u000afibrofatty tissue, which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3.2cm  A short suture is \u000apresent on one surface of the specimen. The surface is inked blue. The \u000aopposite surface is inked orange. Within the specimen at the border opposite \u000athe stitch is a mass, which measures REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm  which has a rubbery \u000aconsistency. Within the mass a focal areas of yellow induration, which \u000ameasures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.2cm  At the border adjacent to the marking suture is a \u000acyst, which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm  Adjacent to the cyst is an area of \u000ahemorrhage, which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm  Note the 0.2cm yellow nodule \u000ais included in micro 23. The area of the marking suture is included cassette \u000a24. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  entire specimen, 15 frags, ESS. \u000aPart three, labeled "#3, medial wall left breast", consists of a portion of \u000afibrofatty tissue, which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm  The portion is roughly \u000aconcaved. The inner surface of the cavity is inked orange. The outer surface \u000ais inked green. Approximately 60% of the specimen consists of white fibrotic \u000atissue. Within the white fibrotic tissue is a single white nodule, which \u000ameasures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.1cm is identified (micro 37). The specimen is serially \u000asectioned and entirely submitted for histological examination. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  entire specimen, 14 frags, ESS. \u000aReports to: OSTEEN, ROBERT, T. M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN \u000a[report_end] 
