aVAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: HOPE E PETERS M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-08- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Ann K Folkins, M.D. \u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aRIGHT BREAST, LOWER OUTER, 8 G STEREOTACTIC CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR \u000aCALCIFICATIONS: \u000aFLORID EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA WITH ATYPIA (block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ; see note). \u000aImmunoperoxidase studies show that some of the cells are immunoreactive for \u000ap63. There is heterogeneous positivity for e-cadherin with some cells \u000aappearing to lack this marker. \u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU is best seen in block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Immunoperoxidase \u000astudies demonstrate that the cells are not immunoreactive for e-cadherin or \u000ap63. \u000aOccasional calcifications are associated with benign epithelium and a \u000asmall intraductal papilloma. \u000aNote: The florid epithelial hyperplasia has a subpopulation of \u000amonomorphic cells that may represent partial involvement by LCIS. The \u000ahyperplasia is not associated with calcifications. Due to the unusual \u000aappearance of the proliferation, this lesion would be evaluated best with \u000aexcision. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHISTORY: Grouped amorphous heterogenous Ca++ right lower/other quadrant. \u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING: \u000a1. Right: Non-palpable calcifications. \u000aLOCATION: \u000a1. Right: lower/outer. \u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY: \u000a1. 8 G Stereotactic vacuum-assisted. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aA/1) Right breast in two orange cassettes - A/with Ca++ and B/without Ca++. \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received in formalin,  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient's name, unit \u000anumber, and "right breast", and consists of two orange cassettes. The first \u000aorange cassette is labeled "A Ca++", and contains multiple yellow/tan cores \u000a(2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm in aggregate). The second orange cassette is labeled "B", \u000aand contains multiple yellow/tan cores (2.2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm in aggregate). \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Orange cassette A contents (Ca++), multi frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Orange cassette B contents, multi frags, ESS. \u000alm/lp \u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08- REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a6/4/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
