aV REMOVED_CASE_ID  MONTEIRO,HEATHER E 49/F <REG REF 10/24> ( REMOVED_CASE_ID ) WIC HOLGERSON,WILLIAM B. M.D.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------Specimen:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : REMOVED_CASE_ID  SOUT Received: 10/24/08- REMOVED_CASE_ID  Spec Type: - Clinical diagnosis & history: Cluster of calcifications, superior left breast, rule out ductal carcinoma in situ; nodule above left nipple REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm , fibroadenoma, rule out carcinoma Edited by: REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.DORD Gross description: The specimen is received in formalin in two containers. Specimen A labeled "stereo biopsies, left breast" contains an orange cassette. Within this orange cassette are three firm, yellowish-pink, glistening needle biopsies ranging in size from 0.5cm  in length x 0.3cm  in diameter to 2.5cm  in length x 0.3cm  in diameter. The specimens are marked with black ink. Also present free floating within the specimen container are three additional soft, yellow needle biopsies ranging in size from 0.5cm  in length x 0.3cm  in diameter to 3.2cm  in length x 0.3cm  in diameter. The specimens are marked with black ink. Section code:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - tissue in orange cassette - 3X all.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - free floating tissue - 3X all. Specimen B labeled "ultrasound guided breast biopsy, left breast at 12 o'clock" consists of two tan-red, firm needle biopsies with a moderate amount of adherent blood clot measuring 1cm  in length, 0.2cm  in diameter and 2.2cm  in length, 0.2cm  in diameter. The specimens are marked with black ink. 2X all. Total fixation time is REMOVED_DATE hours. Dictated by: LV Edited by: REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.DORD DIAGNOSIS: A. Left breast, needle core biopsy: Ductal carcinoma in situ, intermediate grade, solid and cribriform patterns with necrosis and microcalcifications. B. Left breast, needle core biopsy at 12 o'clock: Fibroadenoma with rare microcalcifications. Extremely minute focus of atypical ductal hyperplasia bordering on low grade micropapillary ductal carcinoma in situ; see note. Edited by: REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.TOCC REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  MD.MIHN DESCRIPTIVE COMMENT: NOTE: In specimen B, in the breast tissue adjacent to the fibroadenoma, there is a very small focus of atypical cells that is at least atypical ductal hyperplasia. This focus resembles the ductal carcinoma in situ seen in specimen A. However, given the very small size of this focus, a definitive diagnosis of ductal carcinoma in situ cannot be made. An immunohistochemical stain for estrogen receptors will be performed on specimen A and the results will be reported in an addendum to follow. Final Diagnosis by: Nicole A. Mihok, M.D. Edited by: REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.TOCC REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.TOCC REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  MD.MIHN Notes: REMOVED_DATE In addition to the co-signer, Drs. Misialek, Ross, Feen and Mattia have seen the case and concur with the above written diagnoses. Edited by: REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.TOCC ADDENDUM REPORTAddendum #1 Entered: 10/29/08- REMOVED_CASE_ID  *** ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION *** This report contains an addendum to the original for the purpose of providing additional diagnostic information. The original diagnosis is unchanged. Immunohistochemical staining on the formalin-fixed, paraffin-embedded block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  reveals these results for the ductal carcinoma in situ: Estrogen receptor: POSITIVE (>10% of nuclei stained) Estrogen receptor ( REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) and/or progesterone receptor (PgR 1 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ) is assessed visually by quantitation of the percent of tumor cells staining.Addendum Final: MIHOK,NICOLE MD***** * REMOVED_DATE <10/29/08- REMOVED_CASE_ID > by MD.MIHN Edited by: REMOVED_DATE -  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT.DORDCODES:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - Positive  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - Obstruction, NO  REMO