aVAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final Type: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: MS-08- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE: MS-08- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken: REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit: Same Day Surgery, WACC 3 MEEI MRN: REMOVED_DATE Path Subspecialty Service: Breast-1 Results To: MICHELLE C SPECHT, M.D. Signed Out by: Adriana Dionigi Corben, M.D. CLINICAL DATA: Left breast biopsy with needle localization. FINAL DIAGNOSIS: BREAST (LEFT), EXCISION: 1) LOBULAR NEOPLASIA (LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN-SITU) (SEE NOTE). 2) FOCAL ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, WITHIN THE REGION OF THE HEALING BIOPSY SITE, AWAY FROM THE INKED RESECTION MARGINS. 3) MICROSCOPIC INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMA. 4) MULTIPLE RADIAL SCARS. 5) CALCIFICATIONS IN FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH FLORID USUAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, IN SCLEROSING ADENOSIS AND IN BENIGN LOBULES (SEE NOTE). 6) HEALING BIOPSY SITE. NOTE: Immunostain for E-cadherin supports the diagnosis of lobular carcinoma in-situ. Immunostains for keratin REMOVED_DATE support the diagnosis of florid usual ductal hyperplasia. Multiple levels examined. By his/her signature below, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh,  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME , REMOVE_MRN and "left breast biopsy", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm oriented irregular tan-yellow and tan-white fibrofatty tissue with a needle localization wire in place. The specimen is accompanied by a radiograph and is oriented by the surgeon with a short stitch designating the superior margin and a long stitch designating the lateral margin of the specimen. The specimen is inked as follows: anterior - blue, posterior - black, superior - green, and inferior - yellow. Serial sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm biopsy cavity site with a tan-pink glistening lining and multiple chalky tan-yellow areas measuring up to 0.5cm in greatest dimension. The biopsy cavity site is 0.5cm from the superior margin, 0.8cm from the posterior margin, 1.0cm from the inferior margin, 1.5cm from the anterior margin, 1.1cm from the lateral margin and 2.3cm from the medial margin of the specimen. No other masses or lesions are grossly seen within the remaining parenchyma of the specimen. The specimen is submitted in its entirety along the medial - lateral axis as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial tip of the specimen, trisected.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Two sequential cross-sections.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Single cross-section, which includes the chalky areas.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Four sequential cross-sections, which include the biopsy cavity.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral tip of the specimen, serially sectioned. Final Diagnosis by Adriana Dionigi Corben M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART : Breast (Left), Excision [report_end] 
