aVAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final Type: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: MS-09- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE: MS-09- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken: REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit: Same Day Surgery, WACC 3 Path Subspecialty Service: Breast-3 Results To: KEVIN S. HUGHES, M.D. RACHEL ANN HITT, M.D. GRACE H LIN, M.D. Signed Out by: Adriana Dionigi Corben, M.D. CLINICAL DATA: Left breast lobular neoplasia on core. FINAL DIAGNOSIS: BREAST (LEFT), EXCISION: 1. LOBULAR NEOPLASIA (LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU). 2. FOCAL FLAT EPITHELIAL ATYPIA AND ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA. 3. INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMA. 4. SCLEROSING ADENOSIS. 5. PSEUDOANGIOMATOUS STROMAL HYPERPLASIA. 6. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH FLORID USUAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA AND CALCIFICATIONS. 7. HEALING BIOPSY SITE. BREAST (LEFT, ADDITIONAL CEPHALAD ASPECT), EXCISION: 1. LOBULAR NEOPLASIA (ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA). 2. FOCAL FLAT EPITHELIAL ATYPIA. 3. INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMA. 4. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH FLORID USUAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA AND CALCIFICATIONS. 5. HEALING BIOPSY SITE. BREAST (LEFT, ADDITIONAL TISSUE #2), EXCISION: FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH USUAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA. GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received are 2 containers which are both  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME , REMOVE_MRN. Received fresh, labeled "left breast", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.0cm portion of fibroadipose tissue received with a needle localization wire in place and accompanied by a radiograph. The specimen is received with a short suture designating the anterior aspect, a long suture designating the lateral aspect and a bowtie suture designating the cephalad aspect of the specimen. The specimen is inked for orientation as follows: superior - green, inferior - yellow, anterior - blue, posterior - black. Sectioning reveals dense focally cystic and gritty gray-white fibrous tissue occupying approximately 60% of the cut surfaces. No distinct masses or lesions are grossly identified. The specimen is entirely submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial end margin, en face.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Body of the specimen, sequentially submitted from medial to lateral.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral end margin, en face. Received fresh, labeled "additional cephalad aspect, left breast", is an unoriented REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.3cm portion of fibroadipose tissue, which is partially cauterized on one aspect. This aspect of the specimen is inked blue, and the remainder of the specimen is inked black. Sectioning reveals predominantly gray-white dense fibrous tissue with no masses or lesions grossly identified. The specimen is submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Ends of the specimen.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Body of the specimen, sequentially submitted from one end to the other. Received in formalin,  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME , REMOVE_MRN and "left breast additional tissue #2", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm fragment of tan-white rubbery fibroadipose tissue, which is inked black, serially sectioned and submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Final Diagnosis by Adriana Dionigi Corben M.D., Electronically signed on Tuesday May 12,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 05:24:30PM By his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. PART A: Breast (Left), Excision PART B: Breast (Left Additional), Excision PART C: Breast (Left Additional #2), Excision [report_end] 
