lization wire enters the \u000aanterior aspect of the specimen. The specimen is sectioned from posterior to \u000aanterior in 13 slices. The localization wire ends in slice #5. A clip is in \u000aslice #7. A hemorrhagic biopsy cavity (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 1.5cm ) extends through \u000aslices #5, #6, #7, and #8 and is located at the inferior, lateral, and superior \u000amargins and extends to 0.5cm from the medial, 2.5cm from the posterior and 3 \u000acm from the anterior margin. There is a hemorrhagic cyst (0.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm ) \u000aabutting the inferior and lateral margins and located 0.5cm from the superior, \u000a2.0cm from the medial, 3.0cm from the posterior and 4cm from the anterior \u000amargin. A radiograph is received with the specimen that shows a clip in the \u000aspecimen and calcifications. The entire specimen is submitted. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Posterior margin (perpendicular sections), 5 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #2 and #3, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #4, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #5 and #6, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #7 (with clip), 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slices #8 and #9, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slices #10 and #11, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Slice #12, 1 frag, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Anterior margin (perpendicular sections), 4 frags, ESS. \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . \u000aJUB/jp \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Gilbert Brodsky M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
