resh,  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient's name, unit number, and "final margin superior-medial half of cavity, short superior, long lateral" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.4cm portion of tan-yellow fibroadipose tissue with 2 black stitches designating the superior and lateral margins. The posterior margin is inked black, the anterior blue, the superior orange, and the inferior yellow. The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a well-defined REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm gray-white rubbery area, which comes to within 0.2cm from the anterior, 0.9cm of the posterior, 0.9cm from the superior, 1.5cm of the inferior, 1.5cm from the lateral, and 4.3cm from the medial margins. The remaining cut surface shows focal areas of dense gray-white fibrosis up to 30%. No other gross abnormalities are identified, and representative sections are submitted from medial to lateral as follows: O-Q: Fibrous tissue, with medial margin as O. R-S: Lesion, entirely submitted T: Lateral margin. Received fresh,  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient's name, unit number, and "additional deep margin" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm portion of tan-yellow fibroadipose tissue with no orientation, which is serially sectioned and entirely submitted as U-V. Gross Description by: STEPHANIE KUEHN Resident: DI TIAN, MD, PhD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT -  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO: Barbara Lynn Smith, M.D. Francis James Mcgovern, M.D. Barbara Ann Penn, M.D. PART A: LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLA SENTINEL NODE LEVEL I), EX PART B: BREAST (LEFT), EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART C: BST(LFT INFEROLATERAL HALF OF CAVITY),FINAL SHAVE PART D: BST(LFT SUPEROMEDIAL HALF OF CAVITY), FINAL SHAVED PART E: BREAST (LEFT), DEEP MARGIN 
