aVAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Amend/Addenda \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: GREGORY J KANE M.D. \u000aCASE: BG-06- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000a********** Revised Report ********** \u000aResident: Marianna B Ruzinova, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Christopher P Crum, M.D. \u000aThis report has been revised to correct a typographical error. The diagnosis \u000aremains unchanged. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aA. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST MASS WITH SUTURE": \u000aBreast tissue with biopsy - related changes, focal epithelial \u000ahyperplasia and vascular calcifications. \u000aB. SPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST MASS": \u000aBreast tissue with biopsy related changes, and focal mild epithelial \u000ahyperplasia. \u000aSkeletal muscle with no significant pathologic change. \u000aThis case has been reviewed by Dr. Deborah Dillon, Breast Pathologist, \u000awho concurs. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: Right breast mass - atypical ductal hyperplasia. \u000aOperation: Excision of right breast m ass \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000a1. Right breast mass with suture at medial aspect \u000a2. Breast mass \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in 2 parts, each  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patients \u000aname and unit number. \u000aPart A, labeled "right breast mass", is one disrupted tan/yellow fragment of \u000afibroadipose tissue (3.2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm ) with a localizing wire inserted into \u000ait. There is a surgical suture placed by the surgeon to indicate the medial \u000aaspect, however, there is no additional suture required to fully orient breast \u000aspecimen. Conversation with Dr. Kane's office reveals that the specimen is \u000asupposed to be unoriented. The resection margin is inked black. The specimen \u000ais serially sectioned and entirely submitted for histologic evaluation. \u000aAlso received are two unoriented tan/yellow tissue fragments (1.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm). \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - right breast mass, 6 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - additional fragments, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aPart B, labeled "right breast mass", consists of five unoriented fragments of \u000ayellow/tan fibroadipose tissue (3.4 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.9cm in aggregate). \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  - right breast mass, 6 frags, ESS. \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Christopher P Crum M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aAmendment #1 by Christopher P Crum M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
