aVAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final Type: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: MS-10- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE: MS-10- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken: REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit: MGH Inpatient Path Subspecialty Service: Breast-3 Results To: MICHELE ANNETTE GADD, M.D. Frozen Section Pathologist: Esther Oliva, M.D. Frozen Section Resident: Omer Yilmaz, M.D., Ph.D. Signed Out by: Melinda J Lerwill, M.D. CLINICAL DATA: Right breast DCIS, having mastectomy. FINAL DIAGNOSIS: LYMPH NODE (RIGHT AXILLA, SENTINEL), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 1 LYMPH NODE (0/1). NOTE: Results of immunostains for cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID .3/Cam5.2, cytokeratin 7, and pankeratin on three tissue levels per block support the above interpretation. BREAST (RIGHT), MASTECTOMY AND AXILLARY LYMPH NODE SAMPLING: 1. EXTENSIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU, CYSTIC HYPERSECRETORY AND PREGNANCY-LIKE TYPES. SEE TABLE #1. 2. EXTENSIVE ATYPICAL CYSTIC HYPERSECRETORY HYPERPLASIA AND ATYPICAL PREGNANCY-LIKE HYPERPLASIA. 3. ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA (CONVENTIONAL TYPE) AND FLAT EPITHELIAL ATYPIA. 4. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH ATYPICAL APOCRINE HYPERPLASIA. 5. RADIAL SCARS. 6. MYXOID FIBROADENOMA. 7. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 3 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES (0/3). 8. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 1 INTRAPARENCHYMAL LYMPH NODE (0/1). NOTE: Results of immunostains for calponin, SM-MHC, and p63 support the above diagnosis. TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS #1 DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU TUMOR SIZE: Extensively involving the parenchyma around the centrally-located biopsy site and also extending into the upper outer, lower outer, and upper inner quadrants. GRADE: 2 to 3. CALCIFICATIONS: In the carcinoma in-situ, atypical hyperplasia, and benign changes. MARGIN OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU: The distances to all margins measure 0.2cm or greater. STAINS FOR RECEPTORS: See specimen number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab,  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME , REMOVE_MRN & "right axillary sentinel node", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0.5cm  tan-pink lymph node, which is bisected and entirely frozen as FX#1 and FX#1A. The entire frozen section material in FX#1 is submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and FX#1A in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . Received fresh,  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME , REMOVE_MRN, "right breast simple mastectomy", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4.8cm simple mastectomy specimen, partially surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x 10.9cm irregularly-shaped fragment of tan-pink, wrinkled skin. The skin surface is remarkable for a REMOVED_DATE x 0.4cm well-healed scar, as well as a REMOVED_DATE x 1.7cm everted nipple with focal white-pink areas. The specimen is received with a suture at 1 aspect denoting the 12 o'clock position. The specimen is inked for orientation as follows: Anterior - blue, posterior - black. Serial sectioning from lateral to medial reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.4cm cavity, located at the 12 o'clock position in the mid breast, subjacent to the aforementioned skin scar. This cavity comes to 3.6cm from the posterior margin and to 3.5cm from the anterior margin. Dense, nodular parenchyma with multiple clustered small cysts surrounds the biopsy site and extends beyond the biopsy site, particularly in the lateral direction. A lateral intraparenchymal lymph node and several axillary lymph nodes are identified. Representative sections are submitted as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative biopsy cavity with surrounding parenchyma.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Representative posterior margin nearest biopsy cavity.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Fibrous tissue away from biopsy site, upper outer quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Fibrous tissue away from biopsy site, upper inner quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Nipple, coronal section.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Axillary lymph nodes, whole.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : One axillary lymph node, serially sectioned.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Intraparenchymal lymph node, bisected.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper outer quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower outer quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Area around biopsy site, from lateral to medial.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Upper inner quadrant.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lower inner quadrant. INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS: FROZEN SECTION #1 & #1A; (RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE): THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF CARCINOMA. Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M.D., Electronically signed on Tuesday February 02,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 06:22:10PM By his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. PART A: Lymph Node (Right Axilla, "Sentinel"), Excision PART B: Breast (Right), Mastectomy and Axillary Lymph Node Sampling PART C: Cryostat Frozen Section (slide only) [report_end] 
