ED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.0cm portion \u000aof yellow/tan lobulated fat, within which a single tan/pink, rubbery lymph node \u000a(2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.7cm ) is identified and bisected. \u000aMicro 1&2: sentinel lymph node, 2 frags total, ESS. \u000aPart two, labeled "#2 L breast - stitch marks axilla", is a 680-gram, REMOVED_DATE x \u000a18.5 x 3.6cm left simple mastectomy specimen to include a tan/pink skin \u000aellipse (6.2 x 4.2cm ), tan areola (5.2 x 3.2cm ), and an everted nipple (1.5 \u000acm in diameter). Five tan/pink, raised lesions (? scar vs papule), are \u000aadjacent to the nipple, each averaging approximately 0.4cm in greatest \u000adimension. A single stitch is present along the lateral aspect, designated as \u000a"axilla" per the surgeon. A definitive axillary tail is not identified. The \u000adeep margin/fascial plane is inked in black. The specimen is serially \u000asectioned from medial to lateral. A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2.0cm  tan, slightly \u000amembranous lesion (? biopsy cavity), is present between the lower outer and \u000alower inner quadrants, 1.5cm from the deep margin and is devoid of any fat \u000anecrosis or gross tumor. An xray of the specimen is taken and a clip is \u000aidentified cetnrally, 2.4cm from the deep resection margin. Adjacent to and \u000asurrounding the aforementioned cavity is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3.5cm area of \u000atan/white, dense cystic fibrous stroma extending into all quadrants with focal \u000anodularity. The remaining breast tissue consists of yellow/tan lobulated fat \u000aadmixed with strands of tan/white fibrous stroma. No lymph nodes are \u000aidentified within the lateral breast tissue. No other lesions are identified. \u000aMicro 3: nipple and adjacent lesion, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 4&5: probable biopsy cavity in relationship to deep, 2 frags total, RSS. \u000aMicro 6&7: additional probable biopsy cavity, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro 8: lower outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro 9: upper outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro 10: upper inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro 11: lower inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  tissue near clip, multi frags, RSS. \u000aPart three, labeled "#3 right breast, stitch marks axilla", consists of an \u000a850-gram, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4.2cm right simple mastectomy specimen, to include an \u000aoverlying tan/pink skin ellipse (5.4 x 3.5cm ), a pink/tan areola (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) and an everted nipple (1.3cm in diameter). A single stitch is present at \u000athe lateral most aspect designating "axilla" per the surgeon. Axillary tissue \u000ais not identified grossly. The deep/fascial plane is inked black and the \u000aspecimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral. A tan/white, dense \u000acystic, lumpy fibrous lesion is present within the central aspect of the \u000abreast, extending to all quadrants and coming to within 0.5cm of the deep \u000amargin. No other lesions grossly consistent with invasive carcinoma are \u000aidentified. Remaining breast tissue consists predominantly of yellow/tan \u000alobulated fat with tan/white strands of fibrous stroma. No lymph nodes are \u000aidentified within the lateralmost aspect of the breast. \u000aMicro 12: nipple and areola, 1 frag, RSS. \u000aMicro 13: upper outer quadrant fibrous tissue, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro 14: lower outer quadrant fibrous lesion, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro 15: lower inner quadrant fibrous lesion, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro 16: upper inner quadrant with relationship to deep, 2 frags, RSS. \u000aMicro 17: lateral breast tissue, 1 frag, RSS. \u000adfi \u000aReports to: OSTEEN, ROBERT, T. M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES \u000a[report_end] 
