ht breast wire localization breast biopsy", consists of a \u000asingle fragment of pink/yellow fibrofatty tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.9cm \u000awith a needle localization wire in place and two orienting sutures, indicating \u000athe superior margin (short suture), and the lateral margin (long suture). The \u000aspecimen was inked and sectioned to reveal no areas grossly suspicious for \u000ainvasive carcinoma. \u000aMicro #1: Superior margins, en face, RSS, 1 frag. \u000aMicro #2: Inferior margin, en face, RSS, 1 frag. \u000aMicro #3: Lateral margin, en face, RSS, 1 frag. \u000aMicro #4: Medial margin, en face, RSS, 1 frag. \u000aMicro #5: Superficial margin, en face, RSS, 1 frag. \u000aMicro #6: Deep margin, en face, RSS, 1 frag. \u000aMicro #7: Area of calcifications, RSS, 1 frag. \u000aMicro #8: Superior/medial, RSS, 1 frag. \u000aMicro #9: Inferior/medial, RSS, 1 frag. \u000aMicro #10: Lateral, RSS, 4 frags. \u000aMicros #11-15: Remainder of specimen, ESS, 7 frags. \u000aReports to: KAELIN, CAROLYN, MARY M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
