e medial and the new margin side \u000alateral/posterior. The specimen consists of yellow/tan lobulated adipose \u000atissue with a firm nodular excision cavity and an attached tan/white REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm skin ellipse bearing a well-healed 6.0cm longitudinal scar. The specimen \u000ais oriented according to the surgeon's designations. The specimen is inked per \u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; \u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. \u000aThe specimen is serially sectioned from anterior to posterior to reveal 70% \u000ayellow lobulated adipose tissue and 30% white/tan, nodular, firm fibrous/scar \u000atissue. The fibrous tissue is extending to the inferior margin and is present \u000aapproximately 0.4cm from the superior, 0.2cm from the lateral, 0.8cm from \u000athe posterior and 0.8cm from the anterior margins. The cavity is lined by \u000awhite/tan firm tissue. The entire specimen is submitted. A metal clip is \u000afound 0.5cm to the posterior and 0.5cm to the medial margin. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Entire specimen submitted from anterior to posterior, REMOVED_DATE frags \u000aeach, ESS. \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000aAWE/ajb \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian R Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on \u000aWednesday REMOVED_MONTH 01,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 04:29:47PM \u000a[report_end] 
