re two sutures placed by the surgeon to designate the superior \u000aand lateral orientation. A 5.3cm  thin, well-healed scar is present on the \u000askin superior and lateral to the nipple. The deep margin of the specimen is a \u000asmooth fascial plane without grossly identified skeletal muscle. The deep \u000amargin is inked in black and the specimen is serially sectioned. A centrally \u000alocated, white fibrous area (2.1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm ), grossly consistent with a \u000aprevious biopsy cavity is identified. This cavity is grossly within 0.3cm of \u000athe deep inked margin. The specimen is grossly 40% tan/white fibrous tissue \u000aand 60% golden yellow adipose tissue. The lateral portion of the specimen is \u000athinly sectioned and examined. No lymph nodes are identified. Representative \u000asections are submitted for microscopic examination. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Sections of biopsy cavity, medial to lateral, 5 frags, RSS \u000aMicro 8: Skin with scar, 1 frag, rSS \u000aMicro 9: Upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS \u000aMicro 10: Upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS \u000aMicro 11: Lower outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS \u000aMicro 12: Lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS \u000aMicro 13: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS \u000arlr \u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
