reviously inked per the surgeon per pathology protocol (superior red, inferior \u000agreen, medial orange, lateral yellow, anterior blue, posterior black) and \u000aserially sectioned from medial to lateral. The cut surface is tan/yellow and \u000ahomogenous with focal areas of dense white fibrous tissue constituting \u000aapproximately greater than 90% of the breast parenchyma. There is an irregular \u000ared/brown hemorrhagic area (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.6cm ) which abuts the superior and \u000aposterior margins and extends to within 0.6cm from the medial margin, 0.9cm \u000afrom the inferior margin, 1.4cm from the anterior margin, and 2.4cm from the \u000alateral margin. No discrete lesions are grossly identified. The specimen is \u000asubmitted in its entirety. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial margin, 3 frags, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Sequential cross sections, medial to lateral, block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  to \u000ainclude hemorrhagic area, blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  to include designated area of \u000amicrocalcifications per specimen radiograph, 1 frag each, ESS. \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral margin, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aCASE NUMBER:  REMOVED_CASE_ID . \u000aSEK/ag \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Vania Nose MD, PhD, Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end] 
