ggregate). A wire is present in the specimen \u000abag, but it is not associated with any part of the specimen. The specimens \u000aare inked, sectioned and entirely submitted for microscopic analysis. \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE - right breast tissue, each fragment bisected, 6 frags, ESS. \u000aPart 2, "right breast tissue", consists of a lump of fibroadipose tissue (1.0 x \u000a0.6 x 0.3cm ) that is inked, bisected and entirely submitted for analysis. \u000aMicro 3 - right breast tissue, 2 frags, ESS. \u000aReports to: KANE, GREGORY, J. M.D. \u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES) \u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS \u000a[report_end] 
