aVAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final Type: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: MS-09- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE: MS-09- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken: REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit: Same Day Surgery Unit Path Subspecialty Service: Breast-2 Results To: MICHELLE C SPECHT, M.D. Resident: Ritu Ghai, M.D. Signed Out by: John H Eichhorn, M.D. CLINICAL DATA: Bilateral breast calcifications. FINAL DIAGNOSIS: BREAST (RIGHT), NEEDLE-LOCALIZED EXCISION: ATYPICAL DUCT HYPERPLASIA, SINGLE FOCUS, WITH ASSOCIATED CALCIFICATIONS. SEE NOTE. STROMAL SCLEROSIS. CALCIFICATIONS WITHIN BENIGN DUCTULES AND AREAS OF SCLEROSING ADENOSIS. NOTE: The focus of atypical ductal hyperplasia spans 0.15cm and is <0.1cm from the inferior margin of the specimen in slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , where it is best demonstrated. Tissue block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  has been leveled entirely through, revealing scattered microcalcifications within benign ductules and lobules (as well as within the small focus of atypical ductal hyperplasia). Multiple levels were also examined of blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . BREAST (LEFT), NEEDLE-LOCALIZED EXCISION: LOBULAR NEOPLASIA (LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN-SITU), A FEW FOCI. SEE NOTE. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES, WITH EXTENSIVE SCLEROSIS, SCATTERED CALCIFICATIONS, FOCAL SLIGHT USUAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA AND SCLEROSING ADENOSIS. MULTIPLE LEVELS EXAMINED OF BLOCK  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID . NOTE: Immunostains of sections from blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  shows that the lobular carcinoma in-situ cells are negative for the expression of e-cadherin, consistent with the rendered interpretation. GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received are 2 containers which are each  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME , REMOVE_MRN. Received fresh, labeled "right breast biopsy", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.1cm  irregular portion of tan-yellow fibroadipose tissue with a short stitch designating superior and a long stitch designating lateral. The specimen is received with a needle localization wire in place, and accompanied by a specimen radiograph. The specimen is inked as follows: anterior - blue, posterior - black, superior - green, inferior - yellow, and serially sectioned from medial to lateral. Sectioning reveals a lobulated, tan-yellow, fatty cut surface. The specimen is entirely submitted as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial end, en face.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Body of specimen.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral end, en face. Received fresh, labeled "left breast biopsy", is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1.4cm  irregular portion of tan-yellow, fibroadipose tissue with a short stitch designating superior, a long stitch designating lateral and a needle localization wire in place. The specimen is received with a specimen radiograph. The specimen is inked as follows: anterior - blue, posterior - black, superior - green, inferior - yellow, and is serially sectioned from medial to lateral. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a lobulated, tan-yellow, fatty cut surface with interspersed areas of hemorrhage and fibrous tissue. No discrete masses or lesions are identified. The specimen is submitted entirely as follows:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Medial end, en face.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Body of specimen submitted partially from medial to lateral.  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Lateral end, en face. Fellow Review by Ritu Ghai M.D., on Friday REMOVED_MONTH 11,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 05:32:21PM By his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. Final Diagnosis by John H Eichhorn M.D., Electronically signed on Saturday REMOVED_MONTH 12,  REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 01:07:34PM By his/her signature above, the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he/she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses. PART A: Breast (Right), Excision PART B: Breast (Left), Excision [report_end] 
