aVAccession Number:  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status: Final \u000aType: Surgical Pathology \u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy \u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: EVA D. GOMBOS M.D. \u000aCASE: BS-05- REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  \u000a REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  \u000aResident: Russell K Dorer, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPathologist: Andrea L Richardson, M.D., Ph.D. \u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS: \u000aLEFT BREAST, CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR AN ILL-DEFINED AND IRREGULAR REMOVED_DATE CM MASS: \u000aColumnar alteration with flat epithelial ATYPIA, (multiple levels examined). \u000aColumnar change, cysts, and elastotic stroma suggestive of a complex sclerosing \u000alesion. \u000aNOTE: Atypia is evaluated best after excision. \u000aCLINICAL DATA: \u000aHistory: 0.3cm left breast mass. \u000aOperation: None given. \u000aOperative Findings: None given. \u000aClinical Diagnosis: None given. \u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: \u000aThe specimen is received in formalin,  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient's name, unit \u000anumber, and "left breast", in an orange cassette, and consists of multiple, \u000asoft, fragmented, tan/yellow to white tissue cores (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x 0.3cm in \u000aaggregate). \u000aMicro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID : Multi frags, ESS. \u000aDfi/ag \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she \u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated) \u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es) \u000arelated thereto. \u000aResident Review by Russell K Dorer M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on \u000a4/13/ REMOVED_CASE_ID  \u000a[report_end] 
